WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:05.150 line:80%
A network experiment needs a target,
an explanation and a way to stop it.

00:00:08.585 --> 00:00:11.045 line:80%
This desktop application keeps all three

00:00:11.055 --> 00:00:14.695 line:80%
in one window: discovery,
target selection,

00:00:14.705 --> 00:00:18.055 line:80%
scenario notes and start or stop controls.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.130 line:80%
Background workers run in a thread pool;

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.780 line:80%
signals return their results
to the window without blocking it.

00:00:28.565 --> 00:00:32.645 line:80%
Discovery and the scenarios sit
in separate Python modules,

00:00:32.655 --> 00:00:35.715 line:80%
so the window only
coordinates the selections.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.760 line:80%
The lab stays on the desktop:
no live target is used,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.240 line:80%
and nothing is executed for the recording.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.730 line:80%
One window for the whole
experiment: discovery,

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.800 line:80%
the scenario description
and the controls that start and stop it.
